# .claude/test-ignore — the paths whose modification does not warrant this project's test suite.
# Read by stop-gate.sh at the same root the walk already found .claude/test-cmd at. Optional:
# absent means every recorded write arms the gate, which is the behaviour that predates this file.
# The mechanism, the grammar and this repository's day-one list are decided in ADR-0137 (§D2, §D6);
# read it before widening this file.
#
# Grammar and matching semantics, exactly as stop-gate.sh implements them:
#   - One shell glob per line, matched with bash's own `case`, so `*` also spans `/`.
#   - Blank lines, and lines whose first non-blank character is `#`, are skipped; a leading run of
#     blanks is no part of a pattern. There is no trailing-comment stripping — a `#` anywhere else
#     on the line is part of the pattern, because a path may legitimately contain one.
#   - A pattern beginning with `~` is expanded against $HOME first, which lands it in the rule
#     below it.
#   - A pattern ending in `/` means directory prefix: `docs/books/` matches `docs/books/*`.
#   - A pattern beginning with `/` (after that `~` expansion) is matched against the ABSOLUTE
#     recorded path. Every other pattern is matched against the path taken RELATIVE to this root.
#     An absolute or `~`-rooted pattern is the only way to exclude a write landing outside it.
#   - The list EXCLUDES, never includes: the suite is skipped only when EVERY path recorded this
#     session is excluded, so one unlisted path still arms the gate.
#
# Every pattern here must have a real subject. A pattern that matches nothing reads as a working
# exemption while covering nothing (CLAUDE.md rule 9), and assertion SGP17 in
# staging/plugin/scripts/tests/stop-gate-path-predicate.test.sh is what keeps that honest. Add a
# pattern only after mutating one of its subjects has been shown to move no assertion in the suite:
# a grep for path literals over the test files over-states real reads, because it counts strings
# written into temporary fixtures.
#
# ── The mutation-derivation record (plan Task 8, R-11), measured 2026-08-14 ─────────────────────
# THE METHOD, and it is the only one that proves anything: replace a candidate path's content with
# garbage, re-run the FULL suite, and keep the candidate only if NO assertion moves. Every mutation
# below was restored and the restore verified against `git status --porcelain` before the next run
# started; a mutation left in place makes every later run measure the wrong thing, silently.
# THE PERIMETER is the 79 files matched by `staging/plugin/scripts/tests/*.test.sh`, the suite this
# repository's test command runs. `staging/plugin/skills/deep-refactor/tests/` sits outside both
# that glob and this measurement. "Moved nothing" means the sorted PASS/FAIL/SKIP ledger of the
# whole suite, with temporary-directory names normalised, did not change by one character.
